<h2>What NOT to Buy</h2>

<p>Stay away from:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Blurple lights under $50.</strong> Any grow light that looks purple is using outdated 2015 LED tech. They're inefficient and the color makes it impossible to spot plant problems.</li>
  <li><strong>"2000W equivalent" lights for $40.</strong> Real 2000W would cost $200+ and require a dedicated circuit. If it's $40, the "2000W" is a fantasy number. Check the actual wattage in the product description.</li>
  <li><strong>Ring lights marketed as grow lights.</strong> Ring lights are for selfies. The spectrum is wrong and the coverage is tiny. I see these on TikTok shops. Don't fall for it.</li>
</ul>

<h2>The Hack Nobody Tells You</h2>

<p>If you're on a tight budget, buy the Barrina T5 4 pack and set them 4 inches above your plants. At 2 inches, 10W per strip is enough for lettuce. 4 inches is perfect for seedlings and herbs. I grew award winning basil at the county fair using only Barrina T5s and a south facing window supplement.</p>

<p>Window glass filters out 30% of usable light. Even a cheap light doubles what your plants get from a windowsill.</p>

